ition to playing the social media  mogul eisenberg has left his mark on  movies like the double roger dodger the  end of the tour and the squid and the  whale but every great actor has their  cinematic kryptonite and in eisenberg's  case that's batman vs superman dawn of  justice the curly-haired star won a  worst supporting act for razzie for his  performance as lex luthor a role that  was probably better suited for someone  older and more menacing honestly  eisenberg is the worst luther of all  time especially when compared to the  likes of gene hackman and michael  rosenbaum eisenberg was just too loud  and manic to play the man of steel's  arch enemy and honestly he would have  done a far better job as the riddler the  joker putting a new spin on a classic  character was a risky move on  eisenberg's part and sadly it just  didn't pay off  for more than a decade halle berry was  one of the most likable stars in  hollywood she starred in comedies like  boomerang serviceable dramas like losing  isaiah and action spectaculars like  x-men then she delivered an absolutely  devastating gut punch of a performance  in the sad engrossing 2001 indie movie  monsters ball her work is leticia  musgrove the grieving widow of an  executed convict falling in love with  her husband's executioner won bury an  academy award for best actress but the  kind of showy meaty scripts befitting a  newly minted oscar winner didn't follow  for barry after monster's ball barry was  a bond girl and die another day played  storm in another x-men movie and  co-starred in the horror flick gothica  then in 2004 she played the titular  character in the batman spin-off  catwoman the film consists mainly of  barry shredding around gotham city in a  tight flesh-bearing cat suit smirking to  herself as she commits crimes and avoids  capture keith phipps of the av club  wrote catwoman is essentially an excuse  to pose barry in ever skimpier outfits  barry at least tried to save this bomb  of a movie and give it her best andrea  thompson of the spool argued some sort  of acting category should have been  created just for her and the amount of  effort she spent trying to salvage the  unsalvageable putting her all into every  idiotic line oops  my bad barry herself called catwoman a  quote piece of  and a god-awful movie when she accepted  her razzie award for worst actress in  person in the first half of the 1980s  eddie murphy was the hottest star on tv  dominating saturday night live with  hilarious characters like velvet jones  buckwheat and mr robinson then he became  a major movie star headlining classic  comedies of the 80s and 90s including  beverly hills cop trading places coming  to america and the nutty professor after  some box office bombs such as the  adventures of pluto nash and i spy eddie  murphy was back on top of hollywood in  2006. he earned plaudits for his rare  dramatic turn as a tragic 60s r b singer  in the 2006 movie adaptation of musical  dream girls murphy received his first  ever academy award nomination and he was  predicted by oscar pundits and experts  to triumphantly take home a statuette  but then norbit came along apparently  derailing everything don't you think i  realize what's going on here miss murphy  starred in norbit as the titular  character a nerdy doormat who falls into  an abusive relationship with a mean  woman named rasputia lattimore with the  aid of prosthetics and a  cringe-inducing fake accent murphy also  portrayed chinese orphanage caretaker mr  wong and with makeup wigs and a fat suit  played respiration too critics hate it  the fart joke heavy norbit a film with a  9 rating on rotten tomatoes it's also  entirely possible that academy award  voters seeing norbit everywhere thought  twice about checking the box for murphy  alan arkin ultimately won best  supporting actor for little miss  sunshine over murphy  in 2003 it had become something of a  national pastime to rag on gili part  romantic comedy part mob movie